This product includes one file from Chainlit
(https://github.com/Chainlit/chainlit), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0:

    .chainlit/translations/en-US.json

That file is Chainlit 2.12.0's own en-US.json, copied byte for byte and then
MODIFIED. Four values differ from the upstream copy; no other value, key or
line does.

    navigation.newChat.dialog.description   (2026-09-10)

was reworded, because the stock wording warns that starting a new chat clears
the chat history, and this application persists every chat.

    chat.messages.status.used               (2026-09-16)
    chat.messages.status.using              (2026-09-16)

were emptied. Chainlit prints one of them in front of every agent step's name,
and "Used act #1" is a framework log line rather than what this application did;
with the prefix gone, the name the application writes ("searched the library
#1") is the whole label.

    chat.watermark                          (2026-09-16)

was replaced with "Evidence provenance is checked in code. The reasoning is
not." The stock wording, "LLMs can make mistakes. Check important info.", sits
directly under a badge that reports a code-only provenance check of the
evidence, and says less than this application knows about its own answer.

No copyright line is quoted here because the installed chainlit 2.12.0
distribution carries none: it ships neither a LICENSE nor a NOTICE file, and
its package metadata declares only "License: Apache-2.0" and "Author: Willy
Douhard, Dan Andre Constantini". The same provenance is recorded beside the
file, in .chainlit/translations/README.md.
